---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import icon from '../../assets/apps/wordy-gerdy.png';
import readIt from '../../assets/apps/wordy-gerdy-read.png';
import hearIt from '../../assets/apps/wordy-gerdy-hear.png';
import stars from '../../assets/apps/wordy-gerdy-stars.png';
---
<Base title="Wordy Gerdy" description="Wordy Gerdy is a sight word flashcard game for kids in grades 1 to 5. No ads, no accounts, no tracking.">
  <header class="hero">
    <Image src={icon} alt="" width={96} densities={[1, 2]} class="icon" />
    <div>
      <h1>Wordy Gerdy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Sight word practice that's a game. Feed Gerdy the words you can read, and he gobbles them up. Nom nom!</p>
      <p class="soon muted">Coming soon to the App Store and Google Play</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="shots">
    <Image src={readIt} alt="Gerdy the monster smiling after eating a word, with a green speech bubble that says Tasty word!" width={260} densities={[1, 2]} class="shot" />
    <Image src={hearIt} alt="A big Gerdy asking Which word did I say? above three word choices: my, make and help, with a speaker button at the top" width={260} densities={[1, 2]} class="shot" />
    <Image src={stars} alt="End of round: a happy Gerdy, Superstar!, three stars, 3 of 3 on the first try and confetti" width={260} densities={[1, 2]} class="shot" />
  </div>

  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Meet Gerdy.</strong> Every word your child gets right flies into Gerdy's mouth, and he chomps it with a happy munch. Miss one and he says "yuck!", and the word comes back later. Gerdy talks to your child in a speech bubble, so nothing ever covers his face.</li>
    <li><strong>Read it.</strong> Your child reads the card out loud and a grown-up taps Got it or Not yet. Great for reading together.</li>
    <li><strong>Hear it, find it.</strong> Wordy Gerdy says the word and your child taps the match from three look-alike words, all on their own. A speaker button plays it again anytime.</li>
    <li><strong>Grades 1 to 5.</strong> Start with word lists from kindergarten to grade 3, or paste in this week's words from school.</li>
    <li><strong>Feels like a game.</strong> A progress bar, a streak flame, stars for five in a row, and confetti at the end of every round.</li>
    <li><strong>Practice where it counts.</strong> Missed words come back later in the round and lead off the next one.</li>
    <li><strong>Made for every kid.</strong> Big buttons, clear colors, and support for VoiceOver, TalkBack, larger text and Reduce Motion.</li>
    <li><strong>No ads, no accounts, no tracking.</strong> Everything stays on the device. See the <a href="/wordy-gerdy/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Credits</h2>
  <p>Gerdy's munch and "yuck" sounds are from Mixkit. Wordy Gerdy is dedicated to the Hansen Girls and Ashley.</p>

  <h2>Help</h2>
  <p>Questions, ideas or something not working? Email <a href="mailto:support@sillywillyapps.com">support@sillywillyapps.com</a>.</p>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .icon { border-radius: 22px; flex: none; width: 96px; height: 96px; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .soon { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; }
  .shots { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .shot { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  @media (max-width: 420px) { .hero { flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
